Summary classification
- worlddc.no_unconditional_equivalence: ACCEPT sound_only only with a new data-level
  overload that recomputes DC and validates a trivial loop. The existing Bool and
  zero-argument methods remain regression_only behavior and remain unchanged.
- wager.w5_independence_family: REVISE. sound_only is justified only for a new overload
  whose checked canonical decoding identifies the supplied rich/poor encodings with
  richImpl k0 and poorImpl and checks an actual k0 >= 2 conclusion instance. An arbitrary
  unbridged rich/poor candidate pair would be witness_validator, not sound_only.
- reference_models.arbitrarily_large_dc: ACCEPT witness_validator with a complete finite
  candidate overload and recomputation of every nested DC and top-level witness field.
- reference_models.arbitrarily_large_ax_core_discrete: ACCEPT witness_validator only with
  a checked symbolic canonical decoder for the function-equality fields. Partial sampling
  of opaque functions is insufficient.
- reference_models.arbitrarily_large_three_layer: ACCEPT witness_validator under the same
  canonical-decoder condition and full validation of tier1, bridge, world, value, and the
  section-13.2 witness.

A1. worlddc.no_unconditional_equivalence

Lean target
- formal/ERIEC/WorldDC.lean:116-120 is
  ERIEC.WorldDC.no_forward_unconditional: an existential DC Unit witness paired with a
  loop for which World.WldNontrivial is false.
- formal/ERIEC/DC.lean:6-18 defines the DC data and hSelf/hSMC/hAct/hBound fields.
- formal/ERIEC/World.lean:35-44 defines WldNontrivial as a nonzero fixed vector.

Current runtime path
- src/worlddc.jl:25-26 compares two externally supplied Bool summaries.
- src/worlddc.jl:34-36 fixes two unequal Bool examples.
- test/test_worlddc.jl:74-80 exercises summaries and separate counterexample helpers.
These paths do not independently establish a DC or the Lean existential witness.

Required additional path for sound_only
- Add an overload near src/worlddc.jl:25-36 accepting an ERIEState, explicit complete
  finite M/E/C carriers, and an explicit loop encoding.
- Recompute all DC clauses with check_DC(sys, all_M, all_E, all_C), not a DCResult or Bool
  supplied by the caller.
- Require the supplied loop to be the exact zero loop. This proves absence of a nonzero
  fixed vector without adding or relaxing a numerical tolerance.
- The overload validates one concrete forward countermodel. It is sound for the
  existential theorem but is not a decision procedure for every DC/world pair.

Concrete tests in test/test_worlddc.jl
- Positive: the canonical one-element full-relation ERIEState with nonempty boundary and
  exact zeros(Int, 1, 1).
- Negative DC mutation: the same state with an empty boundary, so hBound is false, paired
  with the zero loop.
- Negative conclusion mutation: the valid DC paired with Matrix{Int}(I, 1, 1); the loop
  is nontrivial and is not the forward countermodel.
- Merely passing (true, false) is not evidence for the new method.

Change targets
- src/worlddc.jl:25-36; test/test_worlddc.jl:74-80.
- specs/checker-semantic-manifest.toml:463-472, including basis_log.
- test/test_checker_semantic_manifest.jl:73-83 hard-codes this pilot relation as
