A1. wager.w5_independence_family

Lean target
- formal/ERIEC/Wager/Basic.lean:44-45 defines W5 as all DC states having hinge.card >= k0.
- formal/ERIEC/Wager/Richness.lean:9-26 defines richImpl k0 and proves its W5 instance.
- lines 28-35 define poorImpl and prove not-W5 under 2 <= k0.
- lines 39-41 define W5_indep_all for every k0 satisfying that premise.

Current runtime path
- src/wager.jl:31-39 constructs both hinge sets internally for a finite threshold list.
- test/test_wager.jl:58-60 uses k0=1 only to reject the theorem premise. That is not a
  negative case for the conclusion at a valid k0.

Required additional path for sound_only
- Add an overload near src/wager.jl:31-39 for a single valid k0 and an independently
  supplied canonical encoding of richImpl k0 and poorImpl.
- The decoder must check the complete Fin k0 / Unit carriers and every W5-relevant fixed
  field: rich dc=true at every state, rich hinge=Finset.univ of cardinality k0, poor
  dc=true at its Unit state, and poor hinge cardinality one.
- Evaluate the W5 quantifier on the complete supplied state carriers and require rich W5
  and poor not-W5. Because the decoder ties these encodings to the fixed Lean objects, a
  successful valid-k0 call is a sound theorem instance; a finite set of calls is not an
  exact decision of the universally quantified theorem.
- If the overload accepts arbitrary rich/poor candidates without this canonical bridge,
  classify it witness_validator instead.

Concrete tests in test/test_wager.jl
- Positive: k0=2, rich states Fin 2 with both dc=true and hinge={0,1}, plus the Unit poor
  state with dc=true and hinge={0}.
- Negative positive-witness mutation: retain k0=2 and both rich states but set one rich
  hinge to a singleton, so W5 richImpl fails.
- Negative negative-witness mutation: retain k0=2 but give the poor state a two-element
  hinge, so not-W5 poorImpl fails.
- k0=1 remains a premise rejection test but is not the required semantic negative.

Change targets
- src/wager.jl:31-39; test/test_wager.jl:58-60.
- specs/checker-semantic-manifest.toml:737-746, including basis_log.

