Current checks and missing fields
- src/reference_models.jl:34-70 generates its own fixture. It checks generated carrier
  sizes/multivaluedness, next keys, three update equations, and a small R2 sample.
- It does not accept an independent witness; validate DC; compute hinge; validate the
  complete DynFrame, dc_eq/frame_eq, TotalNext/internal_total, E5, dynamic.stable, or
  same_stable. Its R2 sample covers only two subsets, not every Set(Fin k).

Feasible full validator condition
- The candidate must use a checked symbolic decoder for largeAXCoreDC, largeDynFrame,
  largeTotalNext, largeRefDrift, largeRefExternal, largeRefCore, and largeRefCoreIso.
  Decoder tags plus complete finite carrier tables can establish equality to these closed
  definitions without treating arbitrary opaque functions as equal after samples.
- Validate positive, full nested DC, canonical dc_eq; all frame fields and canonical
  frame_eq; total.next/next_internal; three cards; multivalued; computed hinge;
  internal_total; dynamic.stable identity; R2Prime; E5; and same_stable.
- Without this decoder, exhaustive frame equality/R2 over all Set(Fin k) costs 2^k and is
  not realistic at the existing k=128. Sampling would not validate all fields, so the
  contract must remain complete_only/regression_only rather than claim witness_validator.

Field-level negative mutations
- positive: k=0; dc/dc_eq: noncanonical boundary or relation; frame/frame_eq: wrong phi or
  drift decoder tag; total/internal_total: next(:s0)=:s0; each card: remove a carrier
  item; multivalued: singleton alpha; hinge: empty rho/sigma; r2: drift(false, nonempty)
  returns false; e5: add an external edge without a matching lifted target;
  dynamic.stable/same_stable: reference a distinct stable-candidate digest.

